<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador sells $20 million zero-coupon bonds.</title>
<headline>Ecuador sells $20 million zero-coupon bonds.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador said it sold $20 million in 357-day zero-coupon bonds in an auction held simultaneously on the Quito and Guayaquil stock exchanges.</p>
<p>The bonds were sold at an average discount price of 92.41 and an average yield of 8.27 percent, the Finance Ministry said late Tuesday.</p>
<p>It received bids for a total of $211.99 million.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429, e-mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
